# Configuration for a hydrostatic white dwarf in 3D.
#
# Purpose: find out whether FLASH holds a self-gravitating white dwarf in
# hydrostatic equilibrium, or whether rho_c drifts the way it does in
# Castro (docs/teoria.md Sec 6.8, paper Fig. 1). Field-free, no MHD, no
# seed field -- that is deliberate: the drift is what bounds the
# measurement window, so it is the thing to test first.
#
# EOS: Helmholtz. It is the appropriate white-dwarf EOS available in FLASH
# (degenerate electrons at finite temperature, plus ions and radiation).
# The 1D model handed in is a ztwd structure at a temperature low enough
# that Helmholtz's extra terms are negligible -- flash_crosscheck/
# make_wd_model.py measures that ratio (P_ion/P_deg ~ 1e-3) rather than
# assuming it.

REQUIRES Driver
REQUIRES Grid
REQUIRES physics/Hydro
REQUIRES physics/Eos/EosMain/Helmholtz
REQUIRES physics/Gravity/GravityMain/Poisson/Multipole
REQUIRES Multispecies
REQUESTS IO

# Poisson/Multipole is 3D only, and so is the question being asked.
USESETUPVARS nDim
IF nDim != 3
  SETUPERROR WDHydrostatic needs 3d for Poisson/Multipole. Use: ./setup WDHydrostatic -auto -3d
ENDIF

# One species, He4-like (A=4, Z=2), so mu_e = A/Z = 2 -- the same
# composition as the Castro problem's mu2.net, so the two runs describe
# the same star.
SPECIES HE4

D sim_modelFile     1D model file: comment lines start with '#', then rows of "r density temperature"
PARAMETER sim_modelFile     STRING  "wd_model.dat"

D sim_nSubZones     sub-sampling points per dimension when mapping the 1D model onto 3D cells
PARAMETER sim_nSubZones     INTEGER 3       [1 to ]

D sim_rhoAmbient    ambient density outside the star
PARAMETER sim_rhoAmbient    REAL    1.0e-4  [0 to ]

D sim_tempAmbient   ambient temperature outside the star
PARAMETER sim_tempAmbient   REAL    1.0e7   [0 to ]

D sim_abar          mean nucleon number of the single species
PARAMETER sim_abar          REAL    4.0     [0 to ]

D sim_zbar          mean charge of the single species
PARAMETER sim_zbar          REAL    2.0     [0 to ]

D sim_xctr          x of the stellar centre
PARAMETER sim_xctr          REAL    0.0

D sim_yctr          y of the stellar centre
PARAMETER sim_yctr          REAL    0.0

D sim_zctr          z of the stellar centre
PARAMETER sim_zctr          REAL    0.0

# Global velocity damping, the equivalent of Castro's problem_source.H.
# The Castro reference curve was produced with damping over [0, 20 t_dyn]
# ramping off from 18 t_dyn (its run log states exactly that), so these
# defaults reproduce that run and not the seeded runs' [0, 5] window.

D sim_dampTimescaleTdyn  damping timescale in units of t_dyn; <= 0 disables damping
PARAMETER sim_dampTimescaleTdyn  REAL  0.2   [0 to ]

D sim_dampEndTdyn        time in t_dyn at which damping stops entirely
PARAMETER sim_dampEndTdyn        REAL  20.0  [0 to ]

D sim_dampRampStartTdyn  time in t_dyn at which the smooth ramp-off begins
PARAMETER sim_dampRampStartTdyn  REAL  18.0  [0 to ]

D sim_tDyn               the star's dynamical time, sqrt(R^3/GM), in seconds
PARAMETER sim_tDyn               REAL  0.2879670  [0 to ]
